WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.800
We are just popping on to say a quick hello and share some news.
我们只是想露个面打个招呼，顺便分享一些消息。

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.020
We have a new podcasting partner.
我们有了新的播客合作伙伴。

3
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.280
That's right.
没错。

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:20.540
Starting August 14th, we will be partnering with the Odyssey Broadcasting Company to finish our rewatch and start the next chapter of Office Ladies.
从8月14日开始，我们将与奥德赛广播公司合作，完成我们的重温之旅，并开启《办公室女士》的下一个篇章。

5
00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.380
Yes, it is so exciting.
是的，这太令人兴奋了。

6
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.160
And, you know, I was just home visiting my family in Texas, and I shared this news with them.
而且，你知道吗，我刚回德克萨斯探望了家人，并把这个消息告诉了他们。

7
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:31.700
And my sister asked if this changes anything for our listeners.
我姐姐问这是否会对我们的听众产生什么影响。

8
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:33.360
And I thought that was a really good question.
我觉得这是一个非常好的问题。

9
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.140
The answer is it does not.
答案是不会。

10
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:35.720
That's right.
没错。

11
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:39.880
You will still get your podcast every Wednesday wherever you listen to Office Ladies.
你们依然可以在每周三通过你们收听《办公室女士》的任何平台收听我们的播客。

12
00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:42.940
And, you know, we are already loving everyone at Odyssey,
而且，你知道，我们已经非常喜欢奥德赛的每一个人了，

13
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:53.140
but we also want to thank the folks at Earwolf who we hold near and dear to our hearts for believing in Office Ladies from day one and everyone we worked with at SiriusXM.
但我们也想感谢Earwolf的伙伴们，我们与他们感情深厚，感谢他们从第一天起就相信《办公室女士》，也感谢我们在SiriusXM共事过的每一个人。

14
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:57.660
We will miss you all, and we are so thankful for the friendships we made along the way.
我们会想念你们所有人的，也非常感谢我们一路走来结下的友谊。

15
00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.100
Yeah.
是的。

16
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.780
Now, we are going to need a little transition time, so we're going to take an extended summer break.
现在，我们需要一点过渡时间，所以我们将进行一个较长的暑假休息。

17
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.480
For the next four weeks, we're going to be rerunning episodes.
接下来的四周，我们将重播之前的剧集。

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.040
Cassie had the really fun idea of rerunning our first four episodes from season five.
凯西有个非常有趣的主意，就是重播我们第五季的前四集。

19
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:14.800
Yes.
是的。

20
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:15.780
I loved this.
我很喜欢这个主意。

21
00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.480
I did, too.
我也是。

22
00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:23.040
And we also went back into our mailbag because we thought it might be fun to kick off each rerun with a couple of extra tidbits.
而且我们还翻看了我们的邮件箱，因为我们觉得在每次重播前分享一些额外的小花絮会很有趣。

23
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.020
I love tidbits.
我喜欢小花絮。

24
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:24.640
We do.
我们也喜欢。

25
00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.120
So, I'll start us off.
那么，我先来开个头。

26
00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:26.660
All right.
好的。

27
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.720
So, today we are rerunning Weight Loss Part One.
今天我们要重播的是《减肥（上）》。

28
00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:31.180
Angela, what have you got for us?
安吉拉，你有什么要分享的吗？

29
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:36.620
Well, if you remember, one of the storylines in this episode is about Andy and Angela's wedding.
嗯，如果你还记得的话，这一集的情节之一是关于安迪和安吉拉的婚礼。

30
00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:43.480
Andy is really trying to plan the perfect wedding for Angela, and she just hates every suggestion that he has.
安迪真的在努力为安吉拉策划一场完美的婚礼，但她讨厌他提出的每一个建议。

31
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.160
Well, because she doesn't really want to marry him.
嗯，因为她其实并不想嫁给他。

32
00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:45.780
Well, I know.
我知道。

33
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:45.980
Right.
没错。

34
00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:53.500
And a few folks wrote in to ask if there were any good alts in the candy bag for an Andy talking head.
有一些听众写信来问，在安迪的单人访谈片段中，有没有什么有趣的备选台词。

35
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.020
Okay.
好的。

36
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.900
It's the one where Andy says, every little boy fantasizes about his fairytale wedding.
就是安迪说“每个小男孩都幻想过自己的童话婚礼”的那一段。

37
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.300
Yes, I remember this.
是的，我记得这个。

38
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.220
I looked.
我查了一下。

39
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.060
There were a bunch.
有很多备选。

40
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.060
I can't believe I didn't even share them on our first watch of this.
真不敢相信我第一次重温时竟然没分享过这些。

41
00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.820
Here are two alts that really cracked me up.
这里有两个让我笑喷的备选台词。

42
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:13.060
Andy says, am I looking forward to my wedding?
安迪说，我期待我的婚礼吗？

43
00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:13.960
Obbs.
当然（Obbs）。

44
00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.060
Am I looking forward to marrying Angela?
我期待娶安吉拉吗？

45
00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.000
Defs.
绝对（Defs）。

46
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.300
Is she looking forward to marrying me?
她期待嫁给我吗？

47
00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:20.460
Probs.
大概吧（Probs）。

48
00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.040
Not totes paws, though.
不过不是百分之百确定（Not totes paws）。

49
00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.660
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

50
00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:26.860
Very Andy.
非常有安迪的风格。

51
00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:27.600
Very Andy.
真有安迪的风格。

52
00:02:27.820 --> 00:02:28.840
Here's another one.
再来一个。

53
00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.440
I can't stop thinking about our wedding day.
我总是忍不住去想我们的婚礼那天。

54
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.100
I gasp when I see Angela coming down the aisle.
看到安吉拉走过过道时，我倒吸了一口凉气。

55
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:36.780
She's a vision in white.
她穿着白纱，美若天仙。

56
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.740
There's a dove in her hair.
她的头发里还有一只鸽子。

57
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:41.980
I nail the singing of our first dance song.
我完美地唱完了我们的第一支舞曲。

58
00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.860
I do some quick robot moves.
我还跳了几下机械舞。

59
00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:45.020
She's impressed.
她被我迷住了。

60
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.720
The mayor's applauding.
市长也在鼓掌。

61
00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:48.520
I wink at a flower girl.
我向一个小花童眨了眨眼。

62
00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.520
She remembers it forever.
她会永远记住那一刻。

63
00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:56.240
And then I take home my blushing bride and have sex for the first time in eight years.
然后我带着我娇羞的新娘回家，八年来第一次有了性生活。

64
00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:57.560
Wow.
哇。

65
00:02:57.960 --> 00:02:58.200
Yeah.
是啊。

66
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.680
That talking head reminds me a little bit of Dwight's talking head where he talks about being
那个采访片段让我想起了德怀特谈论自己是

67
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.520
the spy.
间谍时的那个采访片段。

68
00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.480
Remember that one that goes like 50 directions?
还记得那个剧情反转了五十次的片段吗？

69
00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:08.340
Yes.
记得。

70
00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:09.900
It has a lot of twists and turns.
那里面有很多曲折离奇的情节。

71
00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:10.940
All right.
好吧。

72
00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.720
Well, lady, I have a little tidbit.
对了，女士，我有个小八卦。

73
00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.720
I saw this letter in our digital mailbag, and it made me chuckle.
我在我们的电子邮箱里看到了这封信，它让我忍俊不禁。

74
00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:19.520
So, you know, in this episode, Pam goes away to art school in New York, and you see Jim
你知道，在这一集中，帕姆去纽约上艺术学校了，你看到吉姆

75
00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.140
and Pam communicating on instant message.
和帕姆在用即时通讯软件交流。

76
00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:22.540
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

77
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.400
Old tech alert.
老古董技术预警。

78
00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.140
And you can see their screen names.
你可以看到他们的网名。

79
00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:34.080
Anna Jo wrote in to say, who came up with the screen names Jim9334 and Receptionitis15?
安娜·乔写信问，吉姆9334和前台炎15这两个网名是谁想出来的？

80
00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:39.480
I will tell you, the answer is John Krasinski.
我来告诉你，答案是约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

81
00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:40.280
Really?
真的吗？

82
00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:45.840
Because John went around to our computers and set up instant message.
因为约翰当时挨个去我们的电脑前设置了即时通讯软件。

83
00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:52.360
When we got the internet, he did this so that we could joke around in the background of scenes.
当我们有了网络后，他这么做是为了让我们能在拍摄背景里开玩笑。

84
00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.220
He did it.
是他做的。

85
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:54.960
Like, they didn't do this in the crew.
剧组人员可没干这事。

86
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.340
And I got to work one day, and he was like, check it out.
有一天我来上班，他说，快看这个。

87
00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:04.020
And he showed me my little instant message screen and that my name was Receptionitis15.
他给我看了我的即时通讯界面，我的名字是前台炎15。

88
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.940
I was like, what is this name?
我说，这是什么鬼名字？

89
00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:06.980
He's like, I don't know.
他说，我也不知道。

90
00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.940
Well, I remember that he talked us through the rest of us how to do it.
嗯，我记得他当时教了我们其他人怎么用。

91
00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:12.300
Yes.
是的。

92
00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.940
Do you remember what your I am screen name was by any chance?
你还记得你的即时通讯网名是什么吗？

93
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:16.420
I do.
记得。

94
00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:20.060
We were so tickled that we could now I am each other during scenes.
我们当时特别高兴，因为终于可以在拍摄间隙互发消息了。

95
00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.540
Mine was MS Accountant.
我的是会计女士。

96
00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:24.940
Ms. Accountant.
会计女士。

97
00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:25.300
Yeah.
没错。

98
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:26.260
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

99
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.400
We really kept on theme for our characters.
我们真的很贴合角色的主题。

100
00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:33.080
Well, listen, we weren't just I aming each other either.
听着，我们可不仅仅是在互发消息。

101
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:37.040
I would I am with fans during scenes.
我当时会和粉丝们在场景里互动。

102
00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.960
Remember when we had MySpace?
还记得我们用MySpace的时候吗？

103
00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:46.700
Somehow, I think I would get the I am of fans through MySpace, and I would write things,
不知怎么的，我觉得我会通过MySpace和粉丝互动，我会写一些东西，

104
00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:58.200
and I would say when you watch the episode Healthcare, there's going to be a scene where Dwight is talking about hot dog fingers, and I aming you during this scene.
我会说，当你们看《医疗保险》那一集时，会有一个德怀特谈论热狗手指的场景，我会在那个场景里和你们互动。

105
00:04:58.420 --> 00:04:58.840
Wow.
哇。

106
00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:00.300
I don't think I had figured that out.
我觉得我当时还没想通这一点。

107
00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:00.840
Yeah.
是啊。

108
00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:03.840
That was something I think BJ Novak might have.
我觉得那可能是BJ·诺瓦克想出来的。

109
00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:04.600
Yeah.
是啊。

110
00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.460
I kind of remember now you guys doing that, and we'd be like, what?
我现在有点想起来你们当时在做那个了，我们当时心想，什么？

111
00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:08.960
You're talking to people right now?
你现在在和别人聊天吗？

112
00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:09.400
Yeah.
是啊。

113
00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:43.510
Yeah.
是啊。

114
00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.150
Just for you.
只为你。

115
00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:51.130
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有我们两个亲历者才能告诉你们的独家幕后故事。

116
00:05:51.310 --> 00:05:52.290
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

117
00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:55.450
Hi, everyone.
大家好。

118
00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:56.270
Hey.
嘿。

119
00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:57.990
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

120
00:05:58.510 --> 00:06:00.130
Why are we screaming already?
我们为什么要尖叫啊？

121
00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.170
We'll tell you.
我们会告诉你们的。

122
00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.270
We are back in the studio.
我们回到录音室了。

123
00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:04.930
We are in the studio.
我们在录音室里。

124
00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:06.430
We are vaccinated.
我们接种过疫苗了。

125
00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:07.710
Our team is vaccinated.
我们的团队也接种过疫苗了。

126
00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:08.550
Look at this.
看看这个。

127
00:06:08.690 --> 00:06:13.790
I can put my arms all the way out to the sides, and I don't touch any clothes or any walls.
我可以把双臂完全向两侧伸展，不会碰到任何衣服或墙壁。

128
00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:17.990
I am not staring at you through my husband's T-shirts or smelling his socks.
我不用再透过我丈夫的T恤盯着你看，也不用闻他的袜子了。

129
00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.130
It's so exciting.
太令人兴奋了。

130
00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:21.830
Lady, I'm looking at your face in real life.
女士，我正在现实生活中看着你的脸。

131
00:06:21.950 --> 00:06:22.410
It's weird.
感觉好奇怪。

132
00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.450
I want to touch it, but I won't.
我想摸摸它，但我不会那么做。

133
00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.430
Can I get you on a Zoom?
我能和你连个Zoom吗？

134
00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.010
Actually, will you go in the other room?
说真的，你能去隔壁房间吗？

135
00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.490
Can we do this over Zoom?
我们能通过Zoom录制吗？

136
00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:33.610
We are thrilled to be here.
我们很高兴能来到这里。

137
00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.110
It's been over a year.
已经过去一年多了。

138
00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:35.870
Over a year?
一年多了？

139
00:06:36.130 --> 00:06:36.310
Yeah.
是啊。

140
00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.390
We don't know what this is going to be, guys.
伙计们，我们不知道这次会是什么样。

141
00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:43.190
We ended up doing more Office Ladies podcasts from our closet than we ever did in person.
我们最终在衣橱里录制的《办公室》女士播客比面对面录制的还要多。

142
00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:44.390
Crazy.
太疯狂了。

143
00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.590
But we're back in person now, and we don't know what's going to happen.
但我们现在又回到线下录制了，不知道会发生什么。

144
00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:50.170
I'll tell you a few changes right off the bat.
我先告诉你们几个变化。

145
00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:54.850
Angela has stopped using note cards, guys, and I'm freaking out.
安吉拉不再用笔记卡了，伙计们，我快崩溃了。

146
00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:55.890
And Post-its.
还有便利贴。

147
00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:58.630
Sam is clapping from the engineer booth.
山姆在工程间里鼓掌呢。

148
00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.390
It's a moment of growth, you guys.
伙计们，这是一个成长的时刻。

149
00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:01.930
I have a Word document now.
我现在有一个Word文档了。

150
00:07:02.030 --> 00:07:02.990
I put everything in.
我把所有东西都放进去了。

151
00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:04.970
It's very adult-y.
这感觉很成熟。

152
00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:06.970
I'm not saying I'm going to stick with it.
我不是说我会一直坚持下去。

153
00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:10.570
Maybe it was something I started doing because I was in my closet, and I just didn't have space
也许我开始这样做是因为我以前在壁橱里，根本没有空间

154
00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:11.290
for all my note cards.
放我所有的笔记卡片。

155
00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:13.210
But look at me at this big table now.
但看看我现在坐在这么大的桌子前。

156
00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:14.270
I know.
我知道。

157
00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.090
It's almost like you want to fill it up with note cards, don't you?
你是不是几乎想用笔记卡片把它填满？

158
