他得穿着西装跑进这场戏，当时真的超级热。

959
00:40:46.390 --> 00:40:53.810
Well, Phil Shea found a cooling vest that Steve could wear under his suit to help keep him cool.
菲尔·谢伊找来了一件冷却背心，让史蒂夫穿在西装里面，帮他降温。

960
00:40:53.810 --> 00:40:57.170
It's the type of vest that marathon runners and athletes have.
那是马拉松运动员和专业选手穿的那种背心。

961
00:40:57.310 --> 00:40:59.350
They use it to cool their body temperature down.
他们用它来降低体温。

962
00:40:59.570 --> 00:41:01.870
It has these little frozen gel packs.
里面有那种小小的冷冻凝胶包。

963
00:41:02.350 --> 00:41:04.130
And Steve had that on under his suit.
史蒂夫当时就在西装里穿了这个。

964
00:41:04.130 --> 00:41:09.530
I've never heard of this thing, which makes sense to me because I would never seek it out.
我从没听说过这玩意儿，这很正常，因为我永远不会主动去寻找它。

965
00:41:09.790 --> 00:41:13.290
I would never think, how can I be colder in any situation?
我从来不会想，在任何情况下我该怎么让自己更冷一点？

966
00:41:13.450 --> 00:41:13.910
No, never.
不，从来不会。

967
00:41:14.050 --> 00:41:14.730
It's a whole thing.
这确实是个专门的东西。

968
00:41:14.870 --> 00:41:15.450
I Googled it.
我谷歌了一下。

969
00:41:15.450 --> 00:41:18.330
There's many different types of cooling vests that you can get.
市面上有很多不同类型的冷却背心。

970
00:41:18.630 --> 00:41:19.550
Athletes use them.
运动员会用。

971
00:41:20.330 --> 00:41:21.490
Soldiers use them.
士兵也会用。

972
00:41:21.790 --> 00:41:23.990
I mean, you know, it's like a whole thing.
我是说，你知道，这确实是个专门的东西。

973
00:41:24.190 --> 00:41:25.230
You know what I do, Owen?
你知道我用什么吗，欧文？

974
00:41:25.430 --> 00:41:25.770
What?
什么？

975
00:41:25.990 --> 00:41:27.130
A warming veSt.
加热背心。

976
00:41:27.490 --> 00:41:30.170
I have a vest and you put little hot packs in it.
我有一件背心，你可以往里面塞那种小暖宝宝。

977
00:41:30.230 --> 00:41:30.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

978
00:41:30.510 --> 00:41:31.570
And it keeps you warm.
它能让你保持温暖。

979
00:41:31.830 --> 00:41:35.490
I bought it so that I could watch my son play ice hockey outdoors.
我买它是为了能看我儿子在户外打冰球。

980
00:41:35.870 --> 00:41:36.250
Yeah.
是啊。

981
00:41:36.530 --> 00:41:39.890
Well, we used to stuff those little hot pocket thingies.
我们以前会塞那种小暖宝宝之类的东西。

982
00:41:39.970 --> 00:41:40.470
What do you call them?
那叫什么来着？

983
00:41:40.930 --> 00:41:42.490
Not the food hot pockets.
不是那种叫“热口袋”的食物。

984
00:41:42.990 --> 00:41:44.030
What are they called?
它们叫什么？

985
00:41:44.130 --> 00:41:47.830
I love the idea of us having a vest filled with hot pockets, though.
不过，我倒是很喜欢我们穿一件塞满“热口袋”背心的主意。

986
00:41:48.050 --> 00:41:51.430
Because then if you get hungry, it's a snack as well.
因为如果你饿了，它还能当零食吃。

987
00:41:51.430 --> 00:41:53.030
It keeps you warm and full.
既能保暖又能填饱肚子。

988
00:41:53.390 --> 00:41:53.690
Listen, listen.
听着，听着。

989
00:41:53.850 --> 00:41:57.790
On the office, I had one skirt that had two little stitch pockets in the back.
在《办公室》剧组时，我有一条裙子，后面有两个小缝口袋。

990
00:41:57.850 --> 00:42:00.610
And I had one little tiny stitch pocket in the front.
前面还有一个极小的缝口袋。

991
00:42:00.810 --> 00:42:03.050
They would give us those little hot pack things.
他们会给我们发那种小暖宝宝。

992
00:42:03.450 --> 00:42:04.250
Little hand warmers?
小暖手宝？

993
00:42:04.450 --> 00:42:05.150
Little hand warmers.
小暖手宝。

994
00:42:05.410 --> 00:42:07.250
I would stick two in my shoes.
我会往鞋子里塞两个。

995
00:42:07.270 --> 00:42:10.030
I would stick one in that front pocket, two in my back pocket.
我会往前面的口袋塞一个，后面口袋塞两个。

996
00:42:10.190 --> 00:42:11.770
I'd stick a few in my bra.
我还会往胸罩里塞几个。

997
00:42:12.130 --> 00:42:12.510
Same.
我也是。

998
00:42:12.630 --> 00:42:13.230
Yeah, I remember that.
是啊，我记得那个。

999
00:42:13.310 --> 00:42:13.450
Yeah.
是啊。

1000
00:42:13.630 --> 00:42:16.030
And if my sweater had pockets, I'd stick them in there.
如果我的毛衣有口袋，我也会把它们塞进去。

1001
00:42:16.270 --> 00:42:20.010
I'd stick so many of those on my body when we were filming outside when it was cold.
以前在户外拍戏天冷的时候，我会在身上贴好多那种暖宝宝。

1002
00:42:20.010 --> 00:42:22.510
One time, our camera operator, Matt Stone, was like,
有一次，我们的摄影师马特·斯通跟我说：

1003
00:42:22.870 --> 00:42:24.410
Ange, just don't take this the wrong way.
安吉，你别误会。

1004
00:42:24.410 --> 00:42:27.050
But I can see lumps in your butt on camera.
但在镜头里，我能看到你屁股上有鼓包。

1005
00:42:27.590 --> 00:42:30.930
Like, they don't look human, like human lumps.
看起来不像人类，不像人类该有的那种鼓包。

1006
00:42:31.210 --> 00:42:32.130
I was like, dang it.
我当时就想，该死。

1007
00:42:32.270 --> 00:42:35.230
And I had to take my little heater things out of my pockets.
我只好把口袋里的小暖宝宝都拿了出来。

1008
00:42:35.590 --> 00:42:38.250
Well, I can't believe that they got a cooling veSt.
话说，真没想到他们竟然弄到了冷却背心。

1009
00:42:38.370 --> 00:42:39.170
And I'm glad they did.
我很高兴他们这么做了。

1010
00:42:39.330 --> 00:42:39.890
I am, too.
我也是。

1011
00:42:39.890 --> 00:42:41.190
I thought that was so smart.
我觉得这主意太棒了。

1012
00:42:41.430 --> 00:42:41.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1013
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:44.170
Well, it's time for another weigh-in.
好了，又到了称重时间。

1014
00:42:44.510 --> 00:42:45.310
Big announcement.
有个重大消息。

1015
00:42:45.310 --> 00:42:47.030
They lost 31 pounds.
他们减掉了31磅。

1016
00:42:47.350 --> 00:42:47.790
Wow.
哇。

1017
00:42:48.230 --> 00:42:49.790
Michael and Holly are so excited.
迈克尔和霍莉太兴奋了。

1018
00:42:49.790 --> 00:42:50.870
They're going to do a wrap.
他们打算包礼物。

1019
00:42:51.090 --> 00:42:52.570
It's the most adorable thing.
这事儿太可爱了。

1020
00:42:52.730 --> 00:42:54.670
Because they're so dorky and cute together.
因为他们俩在一起又呆萌又可爱。

1021
00:42:55.050 --> 00:42:59.130
Well, a little wrap trivia is that they have about 10 minutes of them wrapping.
关于包礼物的小花絮是，他们当时包了大概10分钟。

1022
00:42:59.370 --> 00:43:03.730
Even though the part that you see in the show was completely scripted.
尽管你在剧中看到的那部分是完全照剧本演的。

1023
00:43:04.190 --> 00:43:07.370
Even down to Holly, like, rubbing her jacket.
甚至连霍莉摩擦她夹克的那种细节也是。

1024
00:43:07.510 --> 00:43:07.870
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

1025
00:43:07.930 --> 00:43:08.730
The wiki-wiki-what.
那个什么什么什么的。

1026
00:43:08.810 --> 00:43:09.790
All of that was scripted.
所有这些都是剧本写好的。

1027
00:43:09.830 --> 00:43:10.670
All of that was scripted.
所有这些都是剧本写好的。

1028
00:43:10.670 --> 00:43:12.350
But they did go on and on.
但他们确实演了很久。

1029
00:43:12.630 --> 00:43:17.210
And Amy Ryan gave an interview where she said this was her favorite scene to shoot because
艾米·瑞恩在一次采访中说，这是她最喜欢拍的一场戏，因为

1030
00:43:17.210 --> 00:43:18.430
they had so much fun.
他们玩得太开心了。

1031
00:43:18.670 --> 00:43:20.150
The crew said the same thing.
剧组人员也这么说。

1032
00:43:20.330 --> 00:43:23.450
They said it was so much fun that those two just went off.
他们说当时太好玩了，那两人完全放飞了自我。

1033
00:43:23.550 --> 00:43:26.070
And that the chemistry was just so apparent.
而且那种化学反应显而易见。

1034
00:43:26.270 --> 00:43:32.370
I think this was the scene when they were shooting when they realized, oh, yeah, these
我觉得就是在这场戏拍摄时，他们意识到，噢，没错，就是

1035
00:43:32.370 --> 00:43:32.710
two.
他们俩。

1036
00:43:33.070 --> 00:43:33.510
True love.
真爱。

1037
00:43:33.770 --> 00:43:33.950
Yeah.
没错。

1038
00:43:34.390 --> 00:43:38.710
Well, now it's week three, and there is a new receptionist in town.
好了，现在是第三周，城里来了一位新前台。

1039
00:43:39.130 --> 00:43:40.270
Yes, Ronnie.
没错，罗尼。

1040
00:43:40.730 --> 00:43:43.190
Yeah, Ronnie, played by Dale Raul.
对，罗尼，由戴尔·劳尔饰演。

1041
00:43:43.570 --> 00:43:45.130
She has been in a ton of stuff.
她演过很多作品。

1042
00:43:45.270 --> 00:43:46.830
She was Maxine in True Blood.
她在《真爱如血》里演玛克辛。

1043
00:43:47.050 --> 00:43:48.450
Oh, Maxine Fortenberry.
噢，玛克辛·福滕伯里。

1044
00:43:48.670 --> 00:43:49.630
I love True Blood.
我超爱《真爱如血》。

1045
00:43:49.810 --> 00:43:50.810
She was fantastic.
她演得太棒了。

1046
00:43:51.130 --> 00:43:52.390
Of course, you would know that.
你肯定会知道这个。

1047
00:43:52.510 --> 00:43:52.810
Yes.
没错。

1048
00:43:52.990 --> 00:43:54.950
I have a crossover connection with Dale.
我和戴尔还有过交集。

1049
00:43:55.250 --> 00:43:55.670
Tell me.
快告诉我。

1050
00:43:55.830 --> 00:43:57.970
We were both on Fresh Off the Boat.
我们都参演过《初来乍到》。

1051
00:43:58.370 --> 00:43:59.090
Well, there you go.
好了，就是这样。

1052
00:43:59.270 --> 00:44:02.610
Not Monk, surprisingly, but Fresh Off the Boat.
令人惊讶的是，不是《神探阿蒙》，而是《初来乍到》。

1053
00:44:02.610 --> 00:44:04.530
Well, she will come back in season six.
嗯，她会在第六季回来。

1054
00:44:04.830 --> 00:44:07.170
This is not the last we're going to see of Ronnie.
我们还会再见到罗尼的。

1055
00:44:07.790 --> 00:44:11.290
Meanwhile, we're going to see Pam in her first class.
与此同时，我们要看看帕姆的第一堂课。

1056
00:44:11.570 --> 00:44:12.750
She looks so cute.
她看起来真可爱。

1057
00:44:12.990 --> 00:44:15.390
She has, like, I'm calling it the college ponytail.
她梳着我称之为“大学马尾”的发型。

1058
00:44:15.670 --> 00:44:18.170
She wears this really cute ponytail at school.
她在学校里梳着这个非常可爱的马尾辫。

1059
00:44:18.490 --> 00:44:18.850
All right.
好吧。

1060
00:44:18.950 --> 00:44:21.770
The ponytail is the only thing that's cute about Pam.
马尾辫是帕姆身上唯一可爱的地方。

1061
00:44:22.050 --> 00:44:22.690
Are you kidding?
你在开玩笑吗？

1062
00:44:22.710 --> 00:44:25.390
I thought you looked so cute in all of your college scenes.
我觉得你在所有大学场景里看起来都很可爱。

1063
00:44:25.750 --> 00:44:28.950
Did you notice how young everyone else is in the class?
你注意到班上其他人有多年轻了吗？

1064
00:44:28.970 --> 00:44:30.110
Oh, you stop it.
噢，别说了。

1065
00:44:30.190 --> 00:44:31.950
No, but this was a deliberate choice.
不，但这是一种刻意的选择。

1066
00:44:31.950 --> 00:44:32.790
Well, okay.
好吧，行。

1067
00:44:33.190 --> 00:44:34.850
Pam is in her late 20s.
帕姆已经快三十岁了。

1068
00:44:34.850 --> 00:44:37.490
Do you like how immediately I, like, stand up for my best friend?
你喜欢我这么快就站出来维护我最好的朋友吗？

1069
00:44:37.490 --> 00:44:38.590
I'm like, you stop it.
我就像是在说，别说了。

1070
00:44:38.650 --> 00:44:39.550
You are beautiful.
你很漂亮。

1071
00:44:39.890 --> 00:44:42.230
You look just as young as those other ones.
你看上去和那些人一样年轻。

1072
00:44:42.550 --> 00:44:42.600
That's right.
没错。

1073
00:44:42.650 --> 00:44:43.830
And you are smart.
而且你很聪明。

1074
00:44:44.370 --> 00:44:44.690
Okay.
好的。

1075
00:44:44.730 --> 00:44:45.170
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1076
00:44:45.310 --> 00:44:45.690
You're welcome.
不客气。

1077
00:44:45.970 --> 00:44:48.650
I want you to know I was not being down on myself.
我想让你知道，我并没有看轻自己。

1078
00:44:48.830 --> 00:44:52.070
I was just pointing out a deliberate production choice.
我只是指出一个刻意的制作选择。

1079
00:44:52.670 --> 00:44:57.730
Pam is in her late 20s, and they made sure that everyone in this class, that the background
帕姆快三十岁了，他们确保班上的每个人，那些背景

1080
00:44:57.730 --> 00:44:59.350
performers were all much younger.
演员都年轻得多。

1081
00:44:59.530 --> 00:45:01.450
They're just starting off in college, right?
他们才刚上大学，对吧？

1082
00:45:01.450 --> 00:45:02.910
Pam's going back to school.
帕姆要重返校园了。

1083
00:45:03.050 --> 00:45:08.250
And they did want to create this story for Pam that she is kind of, you know.
他们确实想为帕姆创造这样一个故事，让她显得有点，你知道的。

1084
00:45:09.290 --> 00:45:09.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1085
00:45:09.970 --> 00:45:10.410
I don't know.
我不知道。

1086
00:45:10.410 --> 00:45:10.910
What am I saying?
我在说什么呢？

1087
00:45:10.910 --> 00:45:11.650
What do they call it?
他们管这叫什么来着？

1088
00:45:11.690 --> 00:45:12.830
A non-traditional student.
非传统学生。

1089
00:45:13.070 --> 00:45:13.630
There you go.
这就对了。

1090
00:45:14.090 --> 00:45:16.630
Well, not only that, she's in the wrong class.
嗯，不仅如此，她还上错课了。

1091
00:45:16.630 --> 00:45:17.170
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1092
00:45:17.310 --> 00:45:21.970
The teacher, who was played by Sandra Lowe, Professor Monaghan.
那位由桑德拉·洛饰演的老师，莫纳汉教授。

1093
00:45:22.090 --> 00:45:26.310
She's got that zinger of a joke about Zaf Chancery, you know?
她关于扎夫·钱塞里的那个俏皮话，你记得吗？

1094
00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:27.170
Yeah.
记得。

1095
00:45:27.650 --> 00:45:31.850
Which, by the way, I read a Reddit thread where people were like, that doesn't apply.
顺便说一下，我读过一个Reddit帖子，人们说那根本不适用。

1096
00:45:32.170 --> 00:45:33.150
It's wrong.
那是错的。

1097
00:45:33.510 --> 00:45:33.930
Oh.
噢。

1098
00:45:34.590 --> 00:45:35.310
Oh, my.
天哪。

1099
00:45:35.510 --> 00:45:37.670
Well, Pam does not end up leaving the class.
好吧，帕姆最终没有退课。

1100
00:45:37.670 --> 00:45:38.650
And we got some mail.
我们收到了一些邮件。

1101
00:45:38.790 --> 00:45:41.850
People were like, Pam has been so good about standing up for herself.
大家都在说，帕姆这次坚持自己的立场做得真好。

1102
00:45:42.170 --> 00:45:43.890
Why doesn't she just leave the class?
她为什么不干脆退出这门课呢？

1103
00:45:44.170 --> 00:45:44.810
I don't know.
我不知道。

1104
00:45:44.930 --> 00:45:45.390
I sympathized.
我很同情她。

1105
00:45:46.050 --> 00:45:47.390
I felt like she's new here.
我觉得她毕竟是新来的。

1106
00:45:47.470 --> 00:45:48.450
She feels out of place.
她感到格格不入。

1107
00:45:48.690 --> 00:45:50.090
She just got singled out.
她只是被针对了。

1108
00:45:50.230 --> 00:45:54.130
She's going to tuck her head down and know she'll do it right the next time.
她会选择忍气吞声，并告诉自己下次一定会做好。

1109
00:45:54.130 --> 00:45:59.150
Yeah, but I guess it's going to mean she misses her actual first trial class.
是啊，但我想这意味着她错过了真正的第一节试听课。

1110
00:46:00.830 --> 00:46:04.810
Back in the office, Holly hears this coughing, right?
回到办公室，霍莉听到了咳嗽声，对吧？

1111
00:46:04.990 --> 00:46:06.270
She's at her cubicle.
她当时在自己的工位上。

1112
00:46:06.730 --> 00:46:07.650
Kelly is coughing.
凯莉在咳嗽。

1113
00:46:07.930 --> 00:46:09.030
She sounds sick.
听起来她病了。

1114
00:46:09.270 --> 00:46:12.610
Did you notice on Holly's desk what her nameplate says?
你注意到霍莉桌上的名牌写的是什么了吗？

1115
00:46:12.890 --> 00:46:13.430
Yes.
注意到了。

1116
00:46:14.210 --> 00:46:14.750
Hollis.
霍利斯。

1117
00:46:14.930 --> 00:46:15.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1118
00:46:15.390 --> 00:46:17.850
And then in quotes, Holly P.
然后引号里写着，霍莉·P。

1119
00:46:18.390 --> 00:46:18.930
Flax.
弗拉克斯。

1120
00:46:19.210 --> 00:46:19.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1121
00:46:19.630 --> 00:46:20.710
I did notice that.
我确实注意到了。

1122
00:46:20.710 --> 00:46:21.750
So that's her real name.
所以那是她的真名。

1123
00:46:21.870 --> 00:46:22.610
Her name is Hollis.
她的名字叫霍利斯。

1124
00:46:22.770 --> 00:46:23.310
